#
# Paths the macOS packager must keep even though Craft's own blacklist drops
# them. Craft reads this as a whitelist, and a whitelisted path outranks a
# blacklisted one — utils.filterDirectoryContent skips a file only when it is
# blacklisted AND not whitelisted. Craft's default whitelist is re.compile("^$")
# and matches nothing, so adding to it takes nothing away.
#
# Craft's macOS blacklist opens with "share/icons/.*". That is right for a KDE
# application: those carry breeze compiled into a library and loose icon files
# are dead weight. Ours are not dead weight — the entire interface is drawn with
# this theme, and it exists only as files.
#
# Without it the theme is absent from the bundle, every QIcon::fromTheme falls
# through to the platform icon engine, and on macOS that engine resolves names
# as SF Symbols. AppKit aborts inside NSImageSymbolRepProvider the first time a
# toolbar is painted: the application opened, then died on the first new project
# with "abort() called" and no other explanation. tests/macos/check_identity.py
# fails the build if the theme goes missing again.
#
# Only this application's own themes are rescued. Every other icon directory
# stays excluded, so the image does not grow by the whole of breeze.
share/icons/wunjo.*
